On Sat, 01 Jul 2006 07:50:25 +0200, joe_doufu <joeclark77@gmail.com> wrote:

> Well don't forget, the god opens up that weapon proficiency when they
> give the monk a weapon.  Still, I'm finding that I do more damage with
> my +2 gloves than with my +0 Vorpal Sword.

However, a +7 artefact weapon can do lots of damage, plus may have special  
effects that martial art haven't.
On my first ascencion, i had an early Mojo and kept it as main weapon (d20  
shock damage).
Frost brand is a classical good artefact weapon, too. Strom has drain  
level which one should neglect. When I get Vorpy with monks (and don't  
want to go weaponless), I usually train my skill and keep Vorpy for the  
occasional J.

> Another opinion question: should I be looking for Dexterity gloves to
> make me a super spellcaster in mid-game, or Power gauntlets to lay the
> smack down?

Depends.
It depends on the other armor you have. If you're in iron shoes and  
helmet, don't spell cast.
It depends on the spell you have. If you have no other spellbooks than the  
beginning one, don't spell cast that much.
On average, don't waste an early wish on either gauntlets unless you  
really really wants to (say you have charm monster + magic missile  
+ identify and need the GoD to cast them with 0% failure)...

You can very well find one kind of gauntlets (if not both) in the dungeon.  
Or in the castle armory. Using one wish of the castle wand for gauntlets  
sounds OK for me. Especially since at that point you'll know if you're  
going more for spellcasing or monster bashing.
If you intend to spell cast and are neutral and have enough HPs, an early  
wish should go toward the Eye (if you don't want to be artiwishless).

If you're playing Slash'em, you'll get some gauntlets of dexeterity as  
first aterfact gift so the question is already solved...


